# Design tokens and accessibility

- Use semantic CSS variables (`--color-background`, `--color-text`, `--color-link`, `--color-focus`, etc.). Do not put raw hex values in components.
- Light mode is the current implementation; keep the same variable names so dark mode can remap later. Do not enable automatic `prefers-color-scheme` dark mode until the light system is stable.
- Never remove focus outlines unless replacing them with an equally visible focus indicator using `--color-focus`.
- Prefer native HTML elements before recreating behaviour with ARIA.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` for non-essential motion.
- Accessibility target: WCAG 2.2 AA.
